  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance - Anti-Monopoly Law, through Government of China (P.R.C.)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This $150,000 technical assistance (TA) supported U.S. industry and government objectives through an integrated program of four workshops that addressed China&apos;s implementation of its Anti-Monopoly Law (AML). This TA provided training for Chinese officials on how the provisions of the AML and eventual implementing regulations would be best applied to ensure outcomes that promote the competitive process and secure non-discriminatory treatment for all market participants. The TA Contractor was the U.S. Chamber of Commerce (Washington, DC); the TA grantee was the American Chamber of Commerce (Beijing, China).</narrative>
  </description>
